# NPU model artifacts and the Qualcomm SDK.
#
# Two reasons, not one. Size — a context bundle is gigabytes. And licence: the
# Qualcomm runtime's grant covers redistribution "as incorporated in Your
# software application" and explicitly NOT "on a standalone basis", so a
# checked-in .aar/.so would be standalone redistribution — and would fold
# proprietary code into an MIT repository. Gradle resolves it from Maven at
# build time instead. See docs/NPU-BACKEND.md.
*.bin
*.pte
*.serialized
qairt/
qnn-sdk/
geniex-sdk/
**/npu-artifacts/
.qai-hub/
qai_hub_token*
*.aihub-token

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Claude Code
.claude/
